From e732121b8076b2fed442345550ca47bb2c0f60a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: ath11k: the survey of the channel in use

Two ath11k patches for the survey of the channel a radio is using
(meant for upstream):

- update ar->rx_channel on a channel switch: the channel-switch path
  left it at the old channel (a TODO in ath11k_mac_update_vif_chan), so
  after a CSA or hostapd's switch_chan the survey kept flagging the old
  channel as in use and never refreshed the new one;
- report the measured noise floor of the channel in use: ath11k took it
  from the firmware's bss channel info event, which on IPQ8074 reads
  -108/-109 dBm on 5 GHz and -101/-102 dBm on 2.4 GHz and barely moves
  (the "-109 all the time" Arista's own firmware showed too), while the
  firmware's pdev stats give the channel's measured noise floor (-94 and
  -96 dBm on the C-260 at the same moment).

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile              |  2 +-
 ...pdate-rx_channel-on-a-channel-switch.patch | 35 ++++++++
 ...ed-noise-floor-of-the-channel-in-use.patch | 85 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/104-wifi-ath11k-update-rx_channel-on-a-channel-switch.patch
